Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep pools off PROMETHEUS listeners

Ia5eaaa2be4d7ed6b8855b9cc7d6baf62631754fb added the PROMETHEUS listener
protocol to the wizard, and selecting it turns pool and health monitor
creation off. A PROMETHEUS listener cannot have a default pool, but
nothing stops a user turning them back on, and the edit form still
offers a default pool for an existing PROMETHEUS listener.

Lock the pool and health monitor toggles while the listener protocol
is PROMETHEUS and say why, drop the pool from the request for such a
listener whatever the toggles say, hide the default pool selection
when editing one, and mention the restriction in the protocol help.

The change was written with an AI coding assistant from a description
of the wanted behaviour, then reviewed. Its first revision was tested
in a 2026.1 deployment; this revision was rebased onto the change
above and checked with the unit tests.

